    "title": "One dead after two vehicle crash in Whitehaven - NewsBreak",
    "text": "MEMPHIS, Tenn. — Police are investigating a scene after one man was taken to the hospital and pronounced dead after a Whitehaven car crash near Millbranch Road on Wednesday night. At 7:07 p.m., officers responded to a two-vehicle crash in the 4300 block of Millbranch Road. According to MPD, one vehicle fled the scene before officers arrived. A man was transported to the hospital in critical condition, and he was pronounced dead on the scene. At 8:20 p.m., police said in an alert that all northbound and southbound lanes on Millbranch Road between Janis Drive and Finley Road were closed due to an investigation. According to MPD, the roads are now back open. This is an ongoing investigation. If you have any information that could help police, call CrimeStoppers at 901-528-CASH. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WREG.com.",
